---
import '../../styles/global.css';
import '../../styles/wiki.css';
import trusts from '../../data/trusts.json';
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
    <title>The Cleopatra Trust System — Cleopatra XI Wiki</title>
    <meta name="description" content="Discover how Cleopatra XI reimagines Trust companions with customized AI, support jobs, combat roles, and progression." />
  </head>
  <body>
    <header class="site-header">
      <div class="nav-wrap">
        <a href="/" class="wordmark"><img src="/images/cleopatra-logo.png" alt="Cleopatra XI" class="nav-logo" /></a>
        <button class="menu-toggle" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="main-nav" aria-label="Toggle navigation">☰</button>
        <nav id="main-nav" class="nav-links">
          <a href="/">Home</a>
          <a href="/#news">News</a>
          <a href="/features/">Features</a>
          <a href="/custom-content/">Custom Content</a>
          <a href="/#getting-started">Getting Started</a>
          <a href="/wiki/" aria-current="page">Wiki</a>
          <a href="/#community">Community</a>
          <a class="nav-cta" href="/#getting-started">DOWNLOAD LAUNCHER ↗</a>
        </nav>
      </div>
    </header>

    <section class="wiki-banner">
      <div class="container">
        <span class="wiki-kicker">CLEOPATRA XI WIKI · TRUSTS</span>
        <h1>The Cleopatra <em>Trust System</em></h1>
        <p>Your companions. Reimagined.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <div class="container wiki-shell">
      <aside class="wiki-sidebar">
        <div class="wiki-sidebar-heading">WIKI NAVIGATION</div>
        <a class="wiki-side-link" href="/wiki/">Overview</a>

        <div class="wiki-side-heading">TRUSTS</div>
        <a class="wiki-side-link active" href="/wiki/trust-system/" aria-current="page">The Cleopatra Trust System</a>
        <a class="wiki-side-link" href="/wiki/trusts/">Trust Compendium</a>
        {trusts.map((t) => (
          <a class="wiki-side-link sub" href={`/wiki/trusts/${t.slug}/`}>{t.name}</a>
        ))}

        <div class="wiki-side-heading">JOBS</div>
        <span class="wiki-side-link muted">Job Changes · Coming soon</span>
        <span class="wiki-side-link muted">Abilities · Coming soon</span>
        <span class="wiki-side-link muted">Weapon Skills · Coming soon</span>

        <div class="wiki-side-heading">EQUIPMENT</div>
        <span class="wiki-side-link muted">Artifact Armor · Coming soon</span>
        <span class="wiki-side-link muted">Custom Equipment · Coming soon</span>

        <div class="wiki-side-heading">CONTENT</div>
        <span class="wiki-side-link muted">Endgame · Coming soon</span>
        <span class="wiki-side-link muted">Feretory · Coming soon</span>

        <div class="wiki-side-heading">SYSTEMS</div>
        <span class="wiki-side-link muted">Quality of Life · Coming soon</span>
      </aside>

      <main class="wiki-main">
        <div class="wiki-breadcrumb">
          <a href="/">Home</a> › <a href="/wiki/">Wiki</a> › The Cleopatra Trust System
        </div>

        <section class="wiki-panel wiki-intro" id="introduction">
          <span class="wiki-kicker">A NEW APPROACH TO COMPANIONS</span>
          <h2>More Than Familiar Faces</h2>
          <p>
            Back in 2015, the Cleopatra server was amongts the first servers to have summonable Trusts.
            This was due to the fact that the server had a low population, so having trusts allowed
            players to complete content without having to form parties.  That deisgn language still exists
            today, as Cleopatra is extremely solo friendly.  Because of this, the Trust system including the
            AI, is designed to have the trusts behave more like regular players rather than simple companions.
            The Cleopatra Trust AI has gone through serveral versions and is currently on Version 6.1 and is
            built around a customized gambit system similar to LSB, however, the actions and conditions are
            greatly expanded to allow Trusts to read and react to more battle situations than retail.  For 
            instance, trusts on LSB/Retail can recognize 39 different battle conditions, while Cleopatra Trusts
            can recognize over 60 unique battle conditions.  This allows for unique Trust gameplay such as 
            certain Trusts being completely aware of their current hate levels and making decisions based on 
            that information.  
          </p>
          <p>
            In addition to this, Trusts in Cleopatra XI are designed to be more than companions who simply
            follow you into battle.  Our customized Trust system expands how companions make combat decisions, 
            by allowing you to change certain companions subjobs that completely alters the way they respond to
            their party, and adapt to different roles. The goal is to make each Trust a meaningful choice in your
            adventuring party.
          </p>
          <p>
            Each companion has its own behavior profile. Some systems are available now, while others are being
            expanded as Cleopatra XI develops.
          </p>
        </section>

        <nav class="wiki-tabs" aria-label="Trust system sections">
          <a href="#combat-ai">Combat AI</a>
          <a href="#support-jobs">Support Jobs</a>
          <a href="#roles">Combat Roles</a>
          <a href="#progression">Progression</a>
          <a href="#companions">Companions</a>
        </nav>

        <section class="wiki-panel wiki-section" id="combat-ai">
          <h2>⚙ Customized Combat AI</h2>
          <p>
            Cleopatra XI expands Trust decision-making through custom behavior rules. A companion's priorities
            can account for factors such as party health, positioning, available abilities, and combat conditions.
          </p>
          <ul class="wiki-bullets">
            <li><strong>Healing priorities:</strong> Healers can distinguish between routine healing and emergencies.</li>
            <li><strong>Ability decisions:</strong> Job abilities can be used according to each Trust's combat role.</li>
            <li><strong>Weapon skill selection:</strong> Custom selection modes can create more variety in combat.</li>
            <li><strong>Individual behavior:</strong> Trusts do not all need to share the same decision rules.</li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <section class="wiki-panel wiki-section" id="support-jobs">
          <h2>♟ Unlockable Support Jobs</h2>
          <p>
            Cleopatra XI's Trust support-job system is designed to let you customize certain companions.
            Support jobs are more than a label: they can affect how a Trust fights, heals, and positions itself.
          </p>
          <p>
            Current support-job choices include Red Mage (RDM), Warrior (WAR), Samurai (SAM), and Ninja (NIN),
            with availability and effects determined for each Trust individually.
          </p>
          <ul class="wiki-bullets">
            <li><strong>RDM:</strong> Can emphasize a support-oriented spellcasting profile.</li>
            <li><strong>WAR:</strong> Can support a more aggressive frontline role.</li>
            <li><strong>SAM:</strong> Can support a weapon-skill-focused combat profile.</li>
            <li><strong>NIN:</strong> Can enable extremely aggresive melee behavior relying shadow-based defenses.</li>
          </ul>
          <p>Not every support job or behavior is available to every Trust. Consult each companion's profile for its specific options.</p>
        </section>

        <section class="wiki-panel wiki-section" id="roles">
          <h2>◈ Adaptive Combat Roles</h2>
          <p>
            A Trust's place in battle can change depending on its configuration. For example, a healer configured
            for frontline combat may move closer to the enemy and use different healing priorities than a
            backline-focused version of the same companion.
          </p>
          <p>
            Our longer-term AI design also includes more situational behavior for support companions, such as
            responding to the songs or abilities they need to use. These behaviors are developed on a Trust-by-Trust basis.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section class="wiki-panel wiki-section" id="progression">
          <h2>✦ Trust Progression & Unlocks</h2>
          <p>
            Trust customization is tied to Cleopatra XI's broader progression systems. Feretory is planned
            as a source of permanent Trust-related unlocks, including support-job options and expansions to
            the Trust system.
          </p>
          <p>
            This approach gives adventurers additional goals beyond simply obtaining a companion. Unlock
            requirements, costs, and availability will be documented as the system is finalized.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section class="wiki-panel wiki-section" id="companions">
          <h2>◉ Every Companion Has a Role</h2>
          <p>
            Trusts are not intended to be interchangeable. Each companion's profile can describe its role,
            available support jobs, equipment, combat priorities, spells, job abilities, and weapon skills.
          </p>
          <p>
            Visit the Trust Compendium to explore individual companions and learn how they fit into your party.
          </p>
          <div class="wiki-bottom">
            <a class="wiki-button" href="/wiki/trusts/">EXPLORE THE TRUST COMPENDIUM →</a>
          </div>
        </section>
      </main>
    </div>

    <footer class="footer">
      <div class="container legal">
        Cleopatra XI is an independent fan project and is not affiliated with or endorsed by Square Enix.
      </div>
    </footer>

    <script>
      const toggle = document.querySelector('.menu-toggle');
      const nav = document.querySelector('.nav-links');

      toggle?.addEventListener('click', () => {
        const isOpen = toggle.getAttribute('aria-expanded') !== 'true';
        toggle.setAttribute('aria-expanded', String(isOpen));
        nav?.classList.toggle('open', isOpen);
      });

      nav?.querySelectorAll('a').forEach((link) => {
        link.addEventListener('click', () => {
          nav.classList.remove('open');
          toggle?.setAttribute('aria-expanded', 'false');
        });
      });
    </script>
  </body>
</html>
